Z||000001||Brandon86SE||11-22-2001||12:20 AM||||Actually I'm very interested in this too, 'cause I know that Pioneer has different coloured decks (for the light up display).  I'd like to have a matching orange/red display to the rest of the cars gauges and interior, as opposed to the pale yellow/green it has right now.<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||BlackStang95||11-22-2001||04:47 AM||||In my experiences you're better off buying a new stereo than a new faceplate from the factory...they do this to make money and to discourage theft.  I have seen (most likely stolen) face plates sell on ebay for as little as $10, I suggest checking that out.||||reg||1
Z||000003||BlackStang95||11-22-2001||04:50 AM||||My bad, their even cheaper than that...<BR> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=1299661836" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=1299661836</A> <P>some searching and patience and you should find what youre looking for cheap||||reg||1
Z||000004||deceler8||11-22-2001||08:53 PM||||Another option would be to check if your local police ever auction recovered goods.<P>Face plates are pretty common at our local police auction.||||reg||1
